{"series":{"id":"federal-fiscal-balance::federal-net-per-capita-2017","label":"Federal spending minus revenue per resident · FFY 2017","dataset_id":"frozen-atlas","unit":"current U.S. dollars per resident","scope":"us_states","definition":"Published per-capita balance of payments, using the same matched fiscal allocation method.","denominator":"Publisher’s most current Census population estimates for the associated calendar year; updated population vintages in the 2025 report. Published per-capita cells retained; population not inferred from rounded totals.","reporting_period":"Federal fiscal year 2017 (2016-10-01 through 2017-09-30); 2025 report historical/revised vintage","source_url":"https://rockinst.org/issue-area/bop-2025/","sources":[{"id":"rockefeller-federal-balance-2025","title":"Rockefeller Institute of Government · Giving or Getting? 2025","url":"https://rockinst.org/issue-area/bop-2025/","date":"Released August 1, 2025; FFY 2023 preliminary, FFY 2022 revised; historical 2015–2023 vintage","note":"Primary publisher of matched federal fiscal allocation estimates. Federal-budget totals reconciled using state allocators and proxies. Fifty states; DC and territory estimates excluded and unpublished. Not a federal-government official state tax-burden or USAspending-only dataset.","license":"Publicly accessible publisher report; copyright Rockefeller Institute of Government. No explicit open reuse licence identified. Attribute publisher and report; do not treat PDF/design as public domain."}],"limitations":["Detailed matched receipts/spending are FFY 2023 preliminary estimates. FY 2022 and earlier history retain the 2025 report’s revisions; no FY 2024/2025 federal balance is claimed.","The federal fiscal year is October 1 through September 30; per-capita denominators use publisher Census estimates for the associated calendar year.","DC and territories are outside the published tables for 50 states: DC stays explicitly missing in every fiscal map.","These are a